<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>MOSAIC — review prototype v0.3</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#173c3a;--paper:#f6f3eb;--line:#a4b8ae}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:18px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}
header,main,footer{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:28px 36px}header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
nav{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap}a{color:#155753;text-underline-offset:5px}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #9c5600;outline-offset:5px}
h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.8rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.08;max-width:850px;margin:22px 0 30px}
h2{font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);line-height:1.25;margin-top:64px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:26px}
h3{line-height:1.3;margin:12px 0;font-size:1.18rem}p{max-width:72ch}
.notice{background:#e9dfc9;padding:10px 24px;font-size:13px}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.14em;font-size:13px;margin-top:36px}
.actions{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}.button{display:inline-block;background:var(--ink);color:white;padding:12px 20px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none}
.hub{border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:12px 12px 0 0;padding:20px;text-align:center;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.04em;background:#e3ece5}
.forms{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1px;background:var(--line);border:1px solid var(--line)}
.forms article{padding:24px;background:#fffdf8}.forms p{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:0}.letter{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:50%;width:38px;height:38px;font-weight:750}
.return{margin:0;max-width:none;padding:18px 24px;background:var(--ink);color:white;border-radius:0 0 12px 12px;font-size:16px}
.record{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}
.record>div{padding:24px;background:#e3ece5}.record>div+div{border-left:1px dashed #577c71}.symbol{font-size:32px}.record p{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:0}
.caption,footer{font-size:14px}.caption{color:#435f55}.brand{letter-spacing:.16em}
@media(max-width:720px){header{display:block}nav{margin-top:16px;gap:12px 20px;font-size:15px}header,main,footer{padding:22px}.forms{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.record{grid-template-columns:1fr}.record>div+div{border-left:0;border-top:1px dashed #577c71}}
@media(max-width:460px){.forms{grid-template-columns:1fr}.forms article{padding:20px}.hub{font-size:12px}body{font-size:17px}}
@media print{nav,.notice{display:none}h2{break-after:avoid}.forms article,.record{break-inside:avoid}body{background:white}}
</style></head><body><div class="notice">Review draft v0.3 · Founder direction applied · Accuracy review pending · No participant results</div><header><strong class="brand">MOSAIC</strong><nav aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#what">What it is</a><a href="#how">How it works</a><a href="#record">Your audit trail</a><a href="#start">Start a decision</a></nav></header><main><p class="eyebrow">FOR DECISIONS WITH CONSEQUENCES</p><h1>When the decision matters, make your reasoning visible.</h1><a class="button" href="#start">Start with your decision →</a><h2 id="what">What is MOSAIC?</h2><p>MOSAIC is a framework for people making weighty decisions with incomplete, scattered or conflicting information. Use it to work towards the best-supported choice you can make with the information you have, and keep a reasoned audit trail of how you reached it. You remain responsible for the decision.</p><p><strong>Who is it for?</strong> People facing choices with significant consequences, who want to examine their reasons carefully and be able to explain them later. The starting point is a decision that matters to you.</p><p><strong>What do you produce?</strong> A reasoned audit trail: what you knew at the time, where it came from, assumptions you made, options you considered, why you chose, what remained uncertain and what would make you reconsider. If things go wrong, this record lets you revisit the reasoning in its original context. It does not guarantee a good outcome.</p><p class="actions"><a class="button" href="#start">Start with your decision →</a><a href="#how">Explore the six forms</a></p><h2 id="how">How it works</h2><p>Use six forms of reasoning, revisiting them as gaps emerge. They are not a fixed one-way sequence.</p><section aria-label="Six connected forms of reasoning"><div class="hub">ONE DECISION · SIX CONNECTED FORMS OF REASONING</div><div class="forms"><article><span class="letter" aria-hidden="true">M</span><h3>Meaning</h3><p>What decision are we making? Name the owner, options, desired outcome, deadline and constraints. Produce a clear decision statement.</p></article><article><span class="letter" aria-hidden="true">O</span><h3>Observations</h3><p>What material do we have? Separate observations, reports, inferences and assumptions. Record origins and gaps.</p></article><article><span class="letter" aria-hidden="true">S</span><h3>Structure</h3><p>How does it connect? Link sources to claims and options. Preserve contradictions and shared origins.</p></article><article><span class="letter" aria-hidden="true">A</span><h3>Analysis</h3><p>What does the evidence support? Examine competing explanations and assumptions. Record findings and limits.</p></article><article><span class="letter" aria-hidden="true">I</span><h3>Interpretation</h3><p>What does that mean for our options? Consider consequences, risks and trade-offs, including uncertainty that could change the choice.</p></article><article><span class="letter" aria-hidden="true">C</span><h3>Choice</h3><p>What will we do, and why? Commit to the course best supported in context, and record the reasons, rejected alternatives, uncertainty and review conditions. Targeted inquiry may be warranted when its value justifies its cost.</p></article></div><p class="return">↶ Revisit any form when a gap or new evidence changes the reasoning.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="record"><h2 id="record">Keep the reasons with the choice.</h2><p>A record you can revisit when the outcome is known.</p><div class="record"><div><span class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">◇</span><h3>What you had</h3><p>Information<br>Origins<br>Assumptions</p></div><div><span class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><h3>What you considered</h3><p>Options<br>Consequences<br>Uncertainty</p></div><div><span class="symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</span><h3>What you chose</h3><p>Choice<br>Reasons<br>Review conditions</p></div></div><p class="caption">An editorial view of a decision record—not extra MOSAIC stages or a prescribed template.</p></section><h2 id="start">Start a decision</h2><p>Write: “By [date], [owner] needs to choose between [options], to achieve [outcome], within [constraints].” Then list what you know, its sources and which uncertainty could change the choice. Use the six forms to examine it; retain reasons and review conditions with the choice. This prompt is an editorial aid, not another MOSAIC stage or a prescribed record format.</p><h2 id="limits">About / FAQ</h2><p><strong>Does MOSAIC decide for me?</strong> No. Human judgement and responsibility remain.</p><p><strong>Does it guarantee a good outcome?</strong> No. Preserve what was known at decision time and learn from later outcomes; a reasoned choice can still have an adverse outcome.</p><p><strong>Is it a score?</strong> No canonical numerical scoring method is established here. Existing demonstration counts and weights are teaching devices.</p><p><strong>Why is Analysis also outside MOSAIC?</strong> External analytical work supplies material. Internal Analysis examines structured evidence for this decision. Operational systems implement the chosen action.</p><p><strong>How established is it?</strong> The public framework is developing. This draft explains a founder-confirmed website baseline, not measured effectiveness.</p></main><footer>Editorial prototype based on the founder-confirmed website baseline, 27 September 2026. No information is collected or sent by this page.<details><summary>Reviewer provenance (exclude from participant copy)</summary><p>Core reference v0.2: SHE-2, document core-reference, revision 3995e839-f6b7-40ef-93fd-ec2de31c9b32. Oracle verdict: SHE-3, document oracle-accuracy-review, revision d7fba4d2-71f9-4848-9baa-101926fa7418, covers v0.1, not these v0.3 changes.</p><p>Founder response ff01d42c-a1f2-41e5-ba11-aedb72f31b5e directs consequential-decision positioning, explanatory visuals and omission of the provisional glimpse. Six-form visual: C1–C7. Audit-trail grouping: C2/C3/C6/C12 and editorial record flexibility I1. These visuals are editorial explanations, not new stages. Audience and best-supported-choice wording expresses intended use, not measured effectiveness or guaranteed optimality. Identifiers are recoverable in Paperclip. External navigation is disallowed during assessment.</p></details></footer></body></html>